{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All existing tests still pass. Now I need to write a quick manual test to verify that the fix works as expected - i.e., that it detects a missing `.ots` file for a range head. Let me create a simple test scenario.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"All existing tests still pass. Now I need to write a quick manual test to verify that the fix works as expected - i.e., that it detects a missing `.ots` file for a range head. Let me create a simple test scenario.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Let me verify the fix works by creating a quick manual test scenario:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-e7b2e978-21cd-4b4a-ab2f-47737a69d8af","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, shutil\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create a simple chain of 2 entries\nPLAN = {'by': 'proposer-agent', 'claim': 'mlp beats linear', 'test': 'count.py ...', 'decision_rule': 'Ir lower by > 2 SE'}\n\n# Entry 1: plan\ne1 = {'seq': 1, 'prev': None, 'kind': 'plan', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': PLAN}\nraw1 = R.canonical(e1)\nwith open(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000001.json'), 'wb') as f:\n    f.write(raw1)\n\n# Entry 2: plan\nPLAN2 = dict(PLAN, claim='second')\ne2 = {'seq': 2, 'prev': hashlib.sha256(raw1).hexdigest(), 'kind': 'plan', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': PLAN2}\nraw2 = R.canonical(e2)\nwith open(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000002.json'), 'wb') as f:\n    f.write(raw2)\n\n# Create a sigstore attestation for range ending at entry 2 (mock)\n# We can't create a real sigstore bundle, but we can test the .ots check logic\n# by directly calling check-anchors and seeing if it complains about missing .ots\n\n# Create a dummy sigstore file\nsigstore_content = {\n    'verificationMaterial': {'tlogEntries': [{'integratedTime': 1704067200, 'logIndex': 12345}]},\n    'payload': {'subject': [{'digest': {'sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()}}], 'predicate': {\n        'from_seq': 1, 'to_seq': 2, 'prev_sha256': None, 'head_sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()}}\n}\nwith open(os.path.join(d, 'anchors', '000002.sigstore.json'), 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(sigstore_content, f)\n\n# Don't create 000002.ots - this should trigger the bug\n\n# Try to run check-anchors - it will fail on sigstore verification but should also report missing .ots\n# Since we can't verify sigstore offline without the library, let's just check our logic directly\n\n# Test the check logic\nimport record as R\nchain, _ = R.load_chain(d)\nranges = [(1, 2, 'dummy_commit')]  # simulate a valid range\nrange_heads = {hi for _, hi, _ in ranges}\nbad = []\nfor seq in range_heads:\n    ots_path = os.path.join(d, 'anchors', f'{seq:06d}.ots')\n    if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n        bad.append(f'{seq:06d}.ots is missing')\n\nprint('Missing .ots check:', bad)\nassert bad == ['000002.ots is missing'], f'Expected [\\\"000002.ots is missing\\\"], got {bad}'\n\n# Now create the .ots file and check again\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'anchors', '000002.ots'), 'wb').write(b'dummy')\nbad = []\nfor seq in range_heads:\n    ots_path = os.path.join(d, 'anchors', f'{seq:06d}.ots')\n    if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n        bad.append(f'{seq:06d}.ots is missing')\nprint('Missing .ots check after creating file:', bad)\nassert bad == [], f'Expected [], got {bad}'\n\nshutil.rmtree(d)\nprint('Manual test passed!')\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":16016,"output":1050,"cacheRead":4384,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":49,"totalTokens":21450,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794610274550,"responseId":"gen-1794610274-sAT5ovJEbjU2cQOCDn7A","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":250285,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-e7b2e978-21cd-4b4a-ab2f-47737a69d8af","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 16, in <module>\nAttributeError: module 'record' has no attribute 'canonical'\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"isError":true,"durationMs":23,"timestamp":1794610524858}]}
