{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":7755,"output":464,"cacheRead":21920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":214,"totalTokens":30139,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The fix looks correct. The new code:\n1. Collects all range heads (the `to_seq` values from successfully verified sigstore ranges) into a set\n2. For each range head, checks if the corresponding `.ots` file exists\n3. If missing, adds a message like `000002.ots is missing` to the `bad` list\n\nThis will cause `check-anchors` to exit with code 1 and print the error message to stderr as required.\n\nLet me also verify the behavior matches the requirements:\n- ✅ `check-anchors` must exit 1 when the `.ots` proof for any attested range head is missing\n- ✅ It must print a message to stderr containing `NNNNNN.ots is missing` (e.g., `000002.ots is missing`)\n- ✅ With the proof present, the existing behaviour must not change\n- ✅ All existing tests in `record/test_record.py` must still pass\n\nThe fix is complete."}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":7755,"output":464,"cacheRead":21920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":214,"totalTokens":30139,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"The fix is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of the change:\n\n**Change made to `/workspace/record/record.py`:**\n\nAdded a check in `cmd_check_anchors` that verifies every range head (the `to_seq` from successfully verified Sigstore attestations) has a corresponding `.ots` proof file:\n\n```python\n# Check that every range head (sigstore to_seq) has a corresponding .ots proof\nrange_heads = {hi for _, hi, _ in ranges}\nfor seq in range_heads:\n    ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{seq:06d}.ots\")\n    if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n        bad.append(f\"{seq:06d}.ots is missing\")\n```\n\n**Behavior:**\n- If a Sigstore attestation for a range ending at entry N is verified successfully, but `anchors/NNNNNN.ots` is missing, `check-anchors` now exits with code 1 and prints `NNNNNN.ots is missing` to stderr\n- If the `.ots` file is present, behavior is unchanged\n- All 20 existing tests pass"}}
