ssing `.ots` files for range heads attested by `.sigstore.json` files.\n\nLooking at the `cmd_check_anchors` function, I need to:\n1. Collect all the range heads (the `to_seq` values from sigstore attestations, which are the `seq` values from `.sigstore.json` files)\n2. For each range head, check if the corresponding `.ots` file exists\n3. If missing, add to `bad` with the message `NNNNNN.ots is missing`\n\nLet me implement this fix.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"All tests pass. Now I need to understand the bug and implement a fix. The issue is that `check-anchors` doesn't check for missing `.ots` files for range heads attested by `.sigstore.json` files.\\n\\nLooking at the `cmd_check_anchors` function, I need to:\\n1. Collect all the range heads (the `to_seq` values from sigstore attestations, which are the `seq` values from `.sigstore.json` files)\\n2. For each range head, check if the corresponding `.ots` file exists\\n3. If missing, add to `bad` with the message `NNNNNN.ots is missing`\\n\\nLet me implement this fix.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Now I'll implement the fix for the missing `.ots` check in `cmd_check_anchors`.\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-a4677f18-eb5a-460b-95d5-22d2b217c920","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"oldText":"    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit\n    if covered < len(chain):\n        bad.append(f\"entries {covered + 1}-{len(chain)} were never attested by the writer\")","newText":"    # Check that every range head (sigstore to_seq) has a corresponding .ots proof\n    range_heads = {hi for _, hi, _ in ranges}\n    for seq in range_heads:\n        ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{seq:06d}.ots\")\n        if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n            bad.append(f\"{seq:06d}.ots is missing\")\n\n    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit\n    if covered < len(chain):\n        bad.append(f\"entries {covered + 1}-{len(chain)} were never attested by the writer\")"}],"path":"/workspace/record/record.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":17319,"output":748,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":143,"totalTokens":18067,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794610055277,"responseId":"gen-1794610055-vPFETyXrjwBcK4rYMSWj","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":134437,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-a4677f18-eb5a-460b-95d5-22d2b217c920","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /workspace/record/record.py."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 407         except Ba